  "question": {
    "text": "In a $\\Delta \\mathrm{PQR}$, if $3 \\sin \\mathrm{P}+4 \\cos \\mathrm{Q}=6$ and $4 \\sin \\mathrm{Q}+3 \\cos \\mathrm{P}=1$, then the angle $\\mathrm{R}$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gz6J0",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{5 \\pi}{6}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6GPgJ",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "xBe9z",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pFY34",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$3 \\sin P+4 \\cos Q=6 \\quad\\dots(1)$\n$4 \\sin Q+3 \\cos P=1\\quad\\dots(2)$\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2) \\angle P$ is obtuse.\n$(3 \\sin P+4 \\cos Q)^2+(4 \\sin Q+3 \\cos P)^2=37$\n$\\Rightarrow 9+16+24(\\sin P \\cos Q+\\cos P \\sin Q)=37$\n$\\Rightarrow 24 \\sin (P+Q)=12$\n$\\Rightarrow \\sin (P+Q)=\\frac{1}{2} \\quad \\Rightarrow P+Q=\\frac{5 \\pi}{6} \\quad \\Rightarrow R=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$",
    "image": null
  },
